From 46037f888f1b8174b0f42c6fd11f4535ec31d904 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 18 Jul 2026 22:09:45 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] v1.6.2: Auto Scan covers all bands (selector) + noise-settle
 fix

Generalizes the 6 GHz Auto Scan to all three radios via a band selector - one
band at a time, a separate report per band, and Pin-best pinning the winner to
that radio.

- 6 GHz: distinct 320 blocks (unchanged; metal-validated in v1.6.1).
- 5 GHz: the 9 non-DFS 20 MHz channels (UNII-1 36-48 + UNII-3 149-165); DFS
  52-144 skipped. Pin-best pins the 80 MHz block around the winner.
- 2.4 GHz: 1 / 6 / 11.

web.c: band-aware rwifi_scan_candidates (per-band enumeration), per-candidate
bandwidth (rwifi_bw_of), scanstart accepts any radio, scan.json carries the
scanned unit. Noise-settle hardening: discard the first post-restart chanim
sample + a 2s settle (fixes the transient -15 dBm knoise seen on metal).

ASP: band selector; band-aware channel/frequency math, spectrum plot (per-band
axis, outside labels for the narrow 20 MHz bars) and report (band in the title);
pinTarget maps a 5 GHz 20 MHz winner to its 80 MHz block.

i18n: RWIF_58 (Band) added; RWIF_30/31/33 made band-generic. 25 dicts, lockstep.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
